|money drop = 600¢ - 2,370¢
}}

==Enemy==
Metal One Horn has one of the fastest attack rates in the game, but has very slow movement speed and pitiful range. He is a mid-tier Metal enemy; while his sizable bulk and rapid attack rate makes him a tough foe for players without any reliable [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]], his low range, speed and health allow most Critical Hitters to make quick work of him. He also tends to appear in non-Metal stages, forcing you to bring a Critical Hitter and waste a valuable slot on a unit that will most likely not help you outside of the Metal One Horn.

==Strategy==
Metal One Horn has much higher HP compared to [[Metal Hippoe]] and [[Metal Doge]], so [[Critical Hit]]s are a must. Since he's outranged by all cats, any Critical Hitter could work in his first appearance, whether it be [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]] or even [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]].

Metal One Horn can demolish your units with his extremely high DPS. If he gets too close for comfort, it is recommended to send out [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster Cat]] and [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Showoff Cat]], which can [[slow]] and [[Freeze|stop]] his movement, respectively. [[Drumcorps Cat (Rare Cat)|Banner Cat]] won't help that much, as his DPS is incredibly high even when [[weaken|weakened]].

